.TH BURNWEB 1 "2026-08-05" "Burn Suite 1.0" "Burn Suite Manual"
.SH NAME
burnweb \- automated web application recon and weakness scanner
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B python3 ./burnweb.py
.br
.B burnweb
.RI ( "if installed via " install.sh )
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B burnweb
fingerprints a web application's tech stack, checks for exposed
sensitive files (\fI.git\fR, \fI.env\fR, backups), fuzzes for hidden
directories, runs nikto for known misconfigurations, checks TLS/cipher
configuration, and flags missing security headers \- all
.B passively
by default.
.PP
Active exploitation (SQL injection testing via sqlmap) is available
but gated behind a separate, explicit, exact\-phrase confirmation at
the end of the scan, plus a second per\-target confirmation. It will
.B never
run without both. See \fBEXPLOITATION GATE\fR below.
.PP
Does not require root.
.SH REQUIREMENTS
.TP
.B python3\-requests
The only hard requirement \- the tool runs its full passive sweep with
just this installed.
.TP
.B nikto, gobuster, sslscan, sqlmap
Each is checked independently at the point of use and skipped
gracefully (with an install hint and a diagnostic code) if missing.
Without gobuster, directory fuzzing falls back to a small built\-in
path list.
.SH USAGE
.TP
.B 1.
Enter a target URL or domain when prompted.
.br
Examples: \fBhttps://example.com\fR, \fBexample.com\fR
.TP
.B 2.
The tool runs all passive checks automatically: fingerprinting,
robots.txt/sitemap, exposed\-file checks, directory fuzzing, nikto,
and a TLS check. Path\-probing checks (exposed files, fallback
directory fuzz) run concurrently for speed.
.TP
.B 3.
If the server returns HTTP 200 for nonexistent paths ("soft\-404"),
path\-existence checks are skipped as unreliable and this is recorded
as a diagnostic rather than silently producing false negatives.
.SS EXPLOITATION GATE
If parameterized URLs or forms were discovered during the passive
sweep, you are shown a large warning and asked to type the exact
phrase
.B "I HAVE PERMISSION"
to proceed. Pressing Enter (or typing anything else) skips
exploitation entirely \- nothing is lost, the report is still
generated with passive findings only.
.PP
If confirmed, you then pick one specific candidate URL from a numbered
list and confirm
.I that exact target
a second time by typing
.BR yes .
Only then does sqlmap run, with conservative settings
(\fB\-\-level=1 \-\-risk=1\fR).
.SH CONFIGURATION
Edit the constants near the top of \fBburnweb.py\fR:
.TP
.B DIR_WORDLIST
Wordlist used by gobuster if installed. Default \fI/usr/share/wordlists/dirb/common.txt\fR.
.TP
.B SQLMAP_ARGS
Arguments passed to sqlmap during the exploitation step. Deliberately
conservative by default \- change with care.
.TP
.B MAX_WORKERS
Concurrent requests used for path\-probing checks against a single
target. Default 8.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Completed normally.
.TP
.B 3
Could not connect to the target over HTTPS or HTTP \- fatal, exits
before any report is written.
.SH DIAGNOSTICS
Every failure, skip, timeout, or empty result is logged to the console
and to the report's DIAGNOSTICS section as a \fBWEB\-NNN\fR code. See
.I ERROR_CODES.txt
in the suite root for the full reference. Notably, a tool timing out
(e.g. nikto after 300s) is logged as a distinct code from that same
tool actually running to completion and finding nothing \- the two are
never conflated.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I burn_report/burnweb_YYYYMMDD_HHMMSS.txt
Generated report for each run.
.SH SECURITY CONSIDERATIONS
.B FOR AUTHORIZED TESTING ONLY.
Only test web applications you own or have explicit written permission
to test. The exploitation gate exists specifically to prevent
accidental unauthorized SQL injection testing \- do not type the
confirmation phrase unless the site owner has authorized active
exploitation. Unauthorized exploitation is a federal crime under the
CFAA and equivalent laws worldwide.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR burnscanner (1),
.BR burncracker (1),
.BR burnrecon (1),
.BR burnreport (1),
.BR burnsuite (7),
.BR nikto (1),
.BR sqlmap (1)
